	(text "RN1 holds every driver input low. The power-on safety of the board\nrests on it: at reset the PCA9554 pins are inputs with a 100 kOhm\npull-up (typical, check). Against 10 kOhm that gives 0.30 V, well\nbelow the 1.4 V a ULN2803A input needs to conduct. The load stays off.\nKeep RN1 next to U4."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 106.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8c5fb2d9-88a8-501d-86ce-58578ff77262")
	)
	(text "COM (pin 10) goes to V_SW, the rail of the loads: the internal\ndiodes then clamp the flyback of each coil. Spec section 4.3."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 121.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "32ddd7bb-950f-5f53-bd29-3743bbea9f6f")
	)
