	(text "Design limits (spec 4.3): 200 mA per channel, 900 mA in total.\nThe PCA9554 drives U4 from 3.3 V: at 200 mA the input needs 2.4 V,\nthe expander gives 2.9 V or more (typical, check).\nPackage: 8 x 0.2 A x 1.1 V = 1.76 W is above the 1.5 W rating.\n1 W derated budget / 1.1 V = 0.9 A in total. F1 holds 1.1 A.\nTwo channels driven together can share one load."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 162.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b5207d87-0d91-5ea7-906f-682969fe7ccc")
	)
	(text "R10 to R17 and R24, by load supply, LED at 2 mA, 2.0 V:\n5 V: 1.5 kOhm.  12 V: 4.7 kOhm.  24 V: 10 kOhm.\nFit the value for the supply used and mark it on the board."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 177.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "84a61371-dce8-5e24-bad1-4f2bb1194290")
	)
	(text "Door strikes above 200 mA: an external relay or two paralleled channels."
